      "text": "\n\n<think>\nThe user wants me to write an incident retrospective for a production API outage caused by a bad cache invalidation rule. Let me structure this carefully with all the requested sections: impact, timeline, contributing factors, detection gaps, remediation, prevention work, and owner handoff. It needs to be 450-550 words, practical language for engineers and managers, concise but complete.\n\nLet me think about what makes a good incident retrospective:\n- Blameless tone\n- Specific technical details that make it feel real\n- Clear timeline with timestamps\n- Actionable items with owners and deadlines\n- Practical language (not overly formal, not too casual)\n- Should feel like something an actual infra team would write\n\nLet me draft this:\n\nTitle: Incident Retrospective \u2013 API Outage Due to Cache Invalidation Rule\n\nI'll structure it with clear headers and keep the language direct. Let me aim for around 500 words.\n\nLet me write it out and count words carefully.\n\n---\n\n**Incident Retrospective: Production API Outage \u2013 Bad Cache Invalidation Rule**\n**Date:** 2025-06-12 | **Severity:** SEV-1 | **Duration:** 47 min | **Incident ID:** INC-2025-0417\n\n**Impact**\nBetween 14:03 and 14:50 UTC, the public-facing /v2/orders and /v2/inventory endpoints returned 503s for approximately 38% of requests. Peak error rate hit 61% at 14:11. Downstream effects: checkout page showed \"temporarily unavailable\" to ~12,400 customers, the mobile app's order-confirmation flow stalled, and the partner integration webhook queue backed up by ~9,000 messages. No data loss. No PII exposure. Revenue impact estimated at $18K in delayed transactions (all completed after recovery).\n\n**Timeline (UTC)**\n- 13:47 \u2013 Deploy #4821 ships a new cache-invalidation rule for the `orders` and `inventory` Redis keys. Rule was intended to purge stale entries on write but used a wildcard pattern (`orders:*:v2`) that matched the active read-through keys instead of the legacy `orders:*:v1` set.\n- 14:03 \u2013 First ",
      "text_preview": "\n\n<think>\nThe user wants me to write an incident retrospective for a production API outage caused by a bad cache invalidation rule. Let me structure this carefully with all the requested sections: impact, timeline, contributing factors, detection gaps, remediation, prevention work, and owner handoff. It needs to be 450",
